<comment datatype='string'>The &lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G-44560&quot;&gt;mdpX&lt;/a&gt; gene of &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-420662&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Methylibium petroleiphilum&lt;/i&gt; PM1&lt;/a&gt;, which is located on the on 600-kb RPME01 megaplasmid, is predicted to encode a 3-hydroxybutanoyl-CoA dehydrogeanse [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/17158667&quot;&gt;Kane07&lt;/a&gt;]. The gene is 1.6-fold upregulated by exposure to &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-19011&quot;&gt;methyl &lt;i&gt;tert&lt;/i&gt;-butyl ether&lt;/a&gt; (MTBE), and thus MdpX was proposed to catalyze the predicted activity of 2-hydroxyisobutanoate-CoA ligase [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/17158667&quot;&gt;Kane07&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/17890343&quot;&gt;Hristova07&lt;/a&gt;].
</comment>
